  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering rural women in the production, processing and marketing of local products.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Niger, the situation of rural women is extremely worrying. Illiterate, and unaware of their rights and those of their children, they are at the mercy of poverty and remain subject to numerous socio-cultural discriminations. Those that have been able to integrate into the agri-food production sectors remain vulnerable due to multiple factors, including a lack of knowledge of certain simple principles likely to secure their investment and increase its value. Community-based organisations such as Transform Niger can play a key role in building the capacity of rural women. This project, submitted by the NGO Transform Niger, will contribute to solving a major problem of socio-economic vulnerability of women members of women&apos;s groups in the localities of Kobi and Louma through specific capacity-building measures including training in market gardening, learning dyeing and manual embroidery. Thanks to your support, Transform Niger will realize its social vision of responsibility by working to empower women and girls, reduce inequalities and fight against gender-based violence. 
KOBI : the women will work on the production and processing of cabbage, tomato, moringa, lettuce and onion on 8,600m2
LOUMA: the women will work on the production and processing of potatoes, tomatoes, parsley and moringa on an 8,800 m2</narrative>
  </description>
